      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "Sinnoh myth says Arceus emerged from an egg in a place where there was nothing at all, then shaped the universe with its 1,000 arms and created Dialga, Palkia and Giratina. People of ancient Hisui worshipped it as 'almighty Sinnoh', which is where the region's name comes from. Its name likely blends arkhē, Greek for 'origin', with Zeus, king of the Greek gods.",
        "guide": "Arceus is a Normal-type Mythical Pokémon that Sinnoh mythology names as the creator of the universe and of Dialga, Palkia and Giratina. Holding one of its Plates, or a type's Z-Crystal, changes it to any of the 18 types. It was worshipped in ancient Hisui as 'almighty Sinnoh'.",
        "tagline": "The Original One, said to have shaped the universe from an egg.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Arceus (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Arceus_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
